From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gentoo-style-arch house patch <noreply@localhost>
Date: Mon, 3 Nov 2026 12:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] meson: don't use libc free_sized()/free_aligned_sized()

The C23 sized-deallocation entry points (glibc 2.43+) are not wrapped by
malloc interposers: tbbmalloc_proxy, mozjemalloc and the Chromium/Electron
allocator shim all export malloc()/free() but not free_sized().  GLib
allocating through the interposed malloc() and then freeing through the
*libc* free_sized() crosses allocators and aborts with "free(): invalid
size" at load time (g_type_class_get -> g_slist_free), taking down every
binary that carries its own allocator (blender, zen/firefox, electron).

Drop the two functions from the probe list so glibconfig.h stays without
G_HAVE_FREE_SIZED and gmem.c compiles its plain free()/aligned_free()
fallbacks, which bind through the interposers like any pre-2.78 GLib.
Measuring: `readelf -Ws libglib-2.0.so.0 | grep UND.free_sized` must be
empty after the rebuild.

---
 meson.build | 10 +++++-----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index 4ce31f0260..5571cbaeb2 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -728,8 +728,6 @@
   'fchmod',
   'fchown',
   'fdwalk',
-  'free_aligned_sized',
-  'free_sized',
   'fsync',
   'ftruncate64',
   'getauxval',
@@ -852,9 +850,11 @@
   endif
 endforeach
 
-# Export the information about free_sized() so we can correctly define a macro
-# wrapper around g_free()/g_free_sized() depending on whether it’s available
-glibconfig_conf.set('G_HAVE_FREE_SIZED', have_func_free_sized)
+# House patch: free_sized()/free_aligned_sized() probing is disabled above —
+# malloc interposers (tbbmalloc_proxy, mozjemalloc, Chromium allocator shim)
+# do not wrap the C23 sized frees, so g_free() must keep its plain free()
+# form (see patch header).
+glibconfig_conf.set('G_HAVE_FREE_SIZED', false)
 
 # Check that stpcpy() is usable; must use header.
 # See:
